  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: psql did not skip in-line COPY ... FROM STDIN data\n     after a COPY that failed before the data phase, so it executed that\n     data as SQL commands (SQL injection via script data)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-6464.patch: count COPY ... FROM STDIN\n       commands in the psql lexer and have SendQuery() discard the data of\n       any that did not reach the COPY-in state; treat an unsolicited\n       COPY_IN result as fatal (upstream commits 5c51ae4556 and\n       f1204c1a79).  Such data must now be terminated by \"\\.\" even when\n       the COPY fails\n     - CVE-2026-6464",
